### Public document sharing
### Routes: /api/shares/*
###
### Create read-only public links to documents with an optional expiry. Fetching a
### shared document by token is public even when auth is enabled; creating, listing
### and revoking shares require auth when it's enabled.

@shareId = REPLACE_WITH_SHARE_ID

### Create a public share (expiry_days optional; service applies defaults/limits)
# @name createShare
POST {{apiUrl}}/shares
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "document_path": "/getting-started",
  "expiry_days": 7
}
# => 201 { "id": ..., "token": ..., "share_url": ..., "expires_at": ... }

### Fetch a shared document by token (public — no auth required)
GET {{apiUrl}}/shares/{{createShare.response.body.token}}
# => 200 the shared document, or 404 if not found / expired

### List shares owned by the current user
# @name listShares
GET {{apiUrl}}/shares
# => 200 { "shares": [...], "total": n }

### Revoke a share by id
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/shares/{{shareId}}
# => 200 { "message": "Share revoked successfully" }

### Clean up all expired shares
POST {{apiUrl}}/shares/cleanup
# => 200 { "message": "Expired shares cleaned up successfully" }

#############################################
### Error cases
#############################################

### Create a share with a missing required document_path
POST {{apiUrl}}/shares
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expiry_days": 7
}

### Fetch a share with a bogus token
GET {{apiUrl}}/shares/not-a-real-token
